    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d449">

                <pb facs="0786" n="716" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg716"/>

                <head>No. 450.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Phelps to Mr.
                    Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1883-09-21"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 21, 1883</date>. (Received
                        October 16.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 6.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge receipt of
                    your dispatch No. 8, with the inclosed copy of Mr. Logan’s note concerning the
                    terms of the proposed treaty of peace as negotiated between Mr. Novoa and
                    General Iglesias.</p>
                <pb facs="0787" n="717" xml:id="pg717"/>
                <p>The importance of the subject-matter of this dispatch is fully recognized, and I
                    shall give it the most earnest and careful attention.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>S. L. PHELPS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
